     ],
     "captions": [
      {
       "t": 0,
       "end": 6.38,
       "text": "Let's look at the parts of the shop a shopper never thinks about, starting with where things are kept."
      },
      {
       "t": 6.88,
       "end": 10.43,
       "text": "The cart service does not store carts itself."
      },
      {
       "t": 10.93,
       "end": 15.78,
       "text": "It keeps them in a fast store that lives in memory, called Valkey."
      },
      {
       "t": 16.09,
       "end": 17.67,
       "text": "That fits."
      },
      {
       "t": 17.99,
       "end": 23.49,
       "text": "A cart is read and written constantly, and losing one costs the shop little."
      }
     ]
    },
    "keeping-the-shop-running-2": {
     "file": "voice/keeping-the-shop-running/keeping-the-shop-running-2.mp3",
     "duration": 12.96,
     "cues": [
      {
       "t": 0,
       "focus": [
        "accounting"
       ]
      },
      {
       "t": 5.39,
       "focus": [
        "ledger_db"
       ]
      }
     ],
     "captions": [
      {
       "t": 0,
       "end": 2.35,
       "text": "An order is different."
      },
      {
       "t": 2.67,
       "end": 4.89,
       "text": "An order is money."
      },
      {
       "t": 5.39,
       "end": 12.64,
       "text": "So accounting writes every order to a real database, PostgreSQL, where it will still be after a restart."
      }
     ]
    },
    "keeping-the-shop-running-3": {
     "file": "voice/keeping-the-shop-running/keeping-the-shop-running-3.mp3",
     "duration": 19.96,
     "cues": [
      {
       "t": 0,
       "focus": [
        "checkout",
        "order_events"
       ]
      }
     ],
     "captions": [
      {
       "t": 0,
       "end": 4.35,
       "text": "And notice what sits between checkout and accounting: a queue."
      },
      {
       "t": 4.67,
       "end": 7.77,
       "text": "They never talk to each other directly."
      },
      {
       "t": 8.09,
       "end": 14.24,
       "text": "If accounting is down for an hour, checkout keeps taking orders, and the messages wait."
      },
      {
       "t": 14.56,
       "end": 19.64,
       "text": "This is why the traces show the queue calling accounting, and not checkout."
      }
     ]
    },
